# The faces never change under a name — only the set grows — so they are cached
# for a year, the same bargain the hand-written routes made before these became
# files. Kept here rather than in the Worker because the Worker no longer sees
# these requests at all.
/icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/icon-512.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/apple-touch-icon-precomposed.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/og.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/door-bg.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/door-bg/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/card-bg/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ---- AND THE THREE FOLDERS THE PICTURES LIVE IN (rome, 2026-09-09: switching
# rooms lags). This file predates the scene art and nobody added them, so every
# plate, every sky and every creature strip was going out as
#
#   cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
#
# which is not "do not cache" — it is worse to feel. The browser HAS the file and
# still has to ask the edge whether it may show it, and wait for the answer. Two
# layers change on a room change, the scene and the sky, so walking through a
# door cost two round-trips before anything could be drawn, plus one more for
# every creature strip the room needed. That is the lag, and it never went away
# with a warm cache, because a warm cache was exactly the case it punished.
#
# THE ?v= IS ALREADY THE CACHE-BUSTER. Every one of these is fetched with
# ?v=ART_V on the end, and the standing rule is that replacing a file means
# bumping ART_V — which changes the URL and therefore the cache entry. So the
# files genuinely are immutable under their names, and always were; the header
# was simply never written down.
#
# IT DOES MAKE THAT RULE LOAD-BEARING. Overwrite a plate without bumping ART_V
# and a year is how long somebody keeps the old one. That was already the rule
# (see scene-art.md) and key-scene.mjs prints the reminder when it replaces a
# file; this is what makes forgetting it expensive.
/room-bg/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/sky/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/mob/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
